{%- doc -%}
  Renders a responsive <img> for a photo that ships in the theme's assets/
  folder, as opposed to one uploaded to Shopify Files.

  Why this exists: every image setting in the stock theme is an image_picker,
  which can only reference a file in Shopify Files - a JSON template has no way
  to point one at a theme asset. Uploading to Files needs the write_files
  Admin API scope, which this store's app doesn't have, so the site's
  photography ships with the theme instead and the blocks that display it reach
  for this.

  Dimensions have to be passed in: Liquid can read width/height off an uploaded
  image object, but an asset is just a filename. Without them nothing reserves
  an aspect ratio and the page reflows as each photo arrives.

  @param {string} photo - Filename of an image in assets/, e.g. 'kcc-big-pour.jpg'
  @param {string} [size] - Its intrinsic size as 'WIDTHxHEIGHT', e.g. '1800x1199'
  @param {string} [alt] - Alt text. Pass '' deliberately for purely decorative photos.
  @param {string} [class] - Class attribute for the <img>
  @param {string} [sizes] - The sizes attribute; defaults to full viewport width
  @param {string} [loading] - 'lazy' (default) or 'eager' for above-the-fold
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign dims = size | default: '' | split: 'x'
  assign intrinsic_width = dims[0] | default: 1800
  assign intrinsic_height = dims[1] | default: 1200
-%}
<img
  src="{{ photo | asset_img_url: '1600x' }}"
  srcset="
    {{ photo | asset_img_url: '400x' }} 400w,
    {{ photo | asset_img_url: '600x' }} 600w,
    {{ photo | asset_img_url: '900x' }} 900w,
    {{ photo | asset_img_url: '1200x' }} 1200w,
    {{ photo | asset_img_url: '1600x' }} 1600w
  "
  sizes="{{ sizes | default: '100vw' }}"
  alt="{{ alt | escape }}"
  width="{{ intrinsic_width }}"
  height="{{ intrinsic_height }}"
  class="{{ class }}"
  loading="{{ loading | default: 'lazy' }}"
>
